Data. The MIT License above covers the code written by our team. It does not
cover the data in data/. The audio clips and transcripts in data/ come from the
Basque Parliament Speech Corpus 1.0 (https://huggingface.co/datasets/gttsehu/basque_parliament_1,
Varona et al., 2024, doi:10.3390/app14051951), which is released under CC0 1.0
(public domain dedication). Our cleaned manifests in data/cleaned/ only select
a subset of that corpus and do not change any transcript. The pretrained models
we evaluate keep their own licences, listed in CITATION.md.
